{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000165","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract foregrounds the Dayhoff Atlas release of datasets and models, so this is primarily a resource paper rather than a standalone model report. It still clearly includes protein-language modeling and protein generation.","evidence_snippet":"“release the Dayhoff Atlas code, datasets, and models” and “generate novel proteins within families”"},{"record_id":"rec_000167","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a causal-interpretability framework applied to existing genomic language models, not a new generative text-bio model. The bridge is analytical rather than a substantive new model bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“training top-k sparse autoencoders on the hidden activations” of “Nucleotide Transformer” and “DNABERT-2”"},{"record_id":"rec_000168","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes fine-tuning GROVER for replication-timing prediction and combining it with epigenetic features, which is a downstream application. It does not establish a generative model, and foundation-model status is only implicit.","evidence_snippet":"“GROVER ... a DNA language model, trained purely on DNA sequence can be fine-tuned for RT”"},{"record_id":"rec_000177","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"MiraST is a new predictive spatial-transcriptomics model with an LLM-derived semantic readout, but the abstract is about prediction rather than generation. Foundation-model evidence is indirect, so it remains unclear.","evidence_snippet":"“LLM-derived semantic gene modulation readout” enabling “zero-shot prediction of unseen genes”"},{"record_id":"rec_000182","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract reads as a broad comparative/architectural discussion of GenAI in clinical decision support, not a primary model paper. It mentions LLMs and GANs, but not evidence of a specific foundation model contribution.","evidence_snippet":"“explores the paradigm shift brought about by Generative Artificial Intelligence” and “architectural comparative analysis”"},{"record_id":"rec_000188","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This studies residual-stream geometry in existing single-cell foundation models rather than proposing a generative text-bio model. The abstract is an analysis of scGPT and Geneformer, not a new architecture.","evidence_snippet":"“residual-stream geometry in scGPT and Geneformer” and “incremental gene-regulatory signal”"}]}
